{"title":"2021 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 22","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1_(Complex_Numbers_and_Vieta&#39;s_Formulas)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1 (Complex Numbers and Vieta's Formulas)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(Complex_Numbers_and_Trigonometric_Identities)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (Complex Numbers and Trigonometric Identities)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(Trigonometric_Identities)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (Trigonometric Identities)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4_(Product-to-Sum_Identity)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4 (Product-to-Sum Identity)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Easy_Video_Solution_by_Scholars_Foundation_Without_Complex_Numbers_and_Euler&#39;s_Identity_(Using_Trigonometry_+_Vieta&#39;s_Formula)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Easy Video Solution by Scholars Foundation Without Complex Numbers and Euler's Identity (Using Trigonometry + Vieta's Formula)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_OmegaLearn_(Euler&#39;s_Identity_+_Vieta&#39;s_Formula)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by OmegaLearn (Euler's Identity + Vieta's Formula)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_grogg007\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by grogg007</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Suppose that the roots of the polynomial <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/e/69ec96efde8d16001510f04f16401e3a945fe848.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(x)=x^3+ax^2+bx+c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"203\" height=\"21\" /> are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/0/550f8fd021a1820a6d85acef4c2ad4d159885931.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos \\frac{2\\pi}7,\\cos \\frac{4\\pi}7,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"115\" height=\"37\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/0/a4033be8971d4656557f590779e43dd14383e853.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos \\frac{6\\pi}7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"53\" height=\"38\" />, where angles are in radians. What is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/a/96a81938ca5e71faa6894d9d52ac776c9efbe75d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$abc$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"27\" height=\"14\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/e/f8e694f6bf3d4057148914431366567270aaf7f2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) }{-}\\frac{3}{49} \\qquad \\textbf{(B) }{-}\\frac{1}{28} \\qquad \\textbf{(C) }\\frac{\\sqrt[3]7}{64} \\qquad \\textbf{(D) }\\frac{1}{32}\\qquad \\textbf{(E) }\\frac{1}{28}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"456\" height=\"43\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_1_.28Complex_Numbers_and_Vieta.27s_Formulas.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1_(Complex_Numbers_and_Vieta's_Formulas)\">Solution 1 (Complex Numbers and Vieta's Formulas)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1 (Complex Numbers and Vieta&#39;s Formulas)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/4/f54d05a7fd9ce7fffa6c13d2bbb834253eed227a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z=e^{\\frac{2\\pi i}{7}}.$\" width=\"67\" height=\"18\" /> Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/3/b13f21416d84e13708696f34dea81026cda583c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> is a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />th root of unity, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/a/d8ac9e217106821552b8d1b8cb6b37f26828f9db.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z^7=1.$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"53\" height=\"15\" /> For all integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/9/c99a6aaebc17474bd09ea71d84d4e769a0662b55.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"17\" height=\"18\" /> note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/9/0c9e523d0dffb1efe0d3ef4141cbc77db0cfbed5.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\cos\\frac{2k\\pi}{7}=\\operatorname{Re}\\left(z^k\\right)=\\operatorname{Re}\\left(z^{-k}\\right).\\]\" width=\"243\" height=\"37\" />\nIt follows that\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/e/31e27c26f87a295aafc7161e87de6d8a7d52c210.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{alignat*}{4} \\cos\\frac{2\\pi}{7} &amp;= \\frac{z+z^{-1}}{2} &amp;&amp;= \\frac{z+z^6}{2}, \\\\ \\cos\\frac{4\\pi}{7} &amp;= \\frac{z^2+z^{-2}}{2} &amp;&amp;= \\frac{z^2+z^5}{2}, \\\\ \\cos\\frac{6\\pi}{7} &amp;= \\frac{z^3+z^{-3}}{2} &amp;&amp;= \\frac{z^3+z^4}{2}. \\end{alignat*}\" width=\"233\" height=\"130\" />\nBy geometric series, we conclude that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/0/350a9cfd23211fb02373142450eb9d14209a4001.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sum_{k=0}^{6}z^k=\\frac{1-1}{1-z}=0.\\]\" width=\"151\" height=\"51\" />\nAlternatively, recall that the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />th roots of unity satisfy the equation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/c/c4c7c71ea2731d6a4affb514e5a4b657ed31fa09.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z^7-1=0.$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"85\" height=\"15\" /> By Vieta's formulas, the sum of these seven roots is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/4/604c735470dd0152ca1cff75fe26eadf5cef7f49.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p>As a result, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/8/7/a87e07d1574685990e32c8fd84b7d8a1d16a839e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sum_{k=1}^{6}z^k=-1.\\]\" width=\"96\" height=\"51\" />\nLet <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/c/31c1db70b7b9fb04d5dfdbec4cf30a52d1e0ba0e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(r,s,t)=\\left(\\cos{\\frac{2\\pi}{7}},\\cos{\\frac{4\\pi}{7}},\\cos{\\frac{6\\pi}{7}}\\right).$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"280\" height=\"43\" /> By Vieta's formulas, the answer is\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/0/a30e7c542402f9221c2fd72ac7d8182f437b187b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} abc&amp;=[-(r+s+t)](rs+st+tr)(-rst) \\\\ &amp;=(r+s+t)(rs+st+tr)(rst) \\\\ &amp;=\\left(\\frac{\\sum_{k=1}^{6}z^k}{2}\\right)\\left(\\frac{2\\sum_{k=1}^{6}z^k}{4}\\right)\\left(\\frac{1+\\sum_{k=0}^{6}z^k}{8}\\right) \\\\ &amp;=\\frac{1}{32}\\left(\\sum_{k=1}^{6}z^k\\right)\\left(\\sum_{k=1}^{6}z^k\\right)\\left(1+\\sum_{k=0}^{6}z^k\\right) \\\\ &amp;=\\frac{1}{32}(-1)(-1)(1) \\\\ &amp;=\\boxed{\\textbf{(D) }\\frac{1}{32}}. \\end{align*}\" width=\"383\" height=\"263\" />\n~MRENTHUSIASM (inspired by Peeyush Pandaya et al)\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28Complex_Numbers_and_Trigonometric_Identities.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(Complex_Numbers_and_Trigonometric_Identities)\">Solution 2 (Complex Numbers and Trigonometric Identities)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (Complex Numbers and Trigonometric Identities)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/4/f54d05a7fd9ce7fffa6c13d2bbb834253eed227a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z=e^{\\frac{2\\pi i}{7}}.$\" width=\"67\" height=\"18\" /> In Solution 1, we conclude that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/1/8e156794db0b3e95d06f8315b3622a9a2027facb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sum_{k=1}^{6}z^k=-1,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -20px\" width=\"97\" height=\"50\" /> so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/8/a/18aec3b04b7459c69d38d90b19abde15646f61a6.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sum_{k=1}^{6}\\operatorname{Re}\\left(z^k\\right)=\\sum_{k=1}^{6}\\cos\\frac{2k\\pi}{7}=-1.\\]\" width=\"251\" height=\"51\" />\nSince <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/9/369107ca6ccdee14ca8f312e7fbeb36795cbb2f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos\\theta=\\cos(2\\pi-\\theta)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"149\" height=\"18\" /> holds for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/2/7f286be9afb0c0eed0725c429ce5247f18229534.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\theta,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"13\" height=\"16\" /> this sum becomes\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/9/3/593c903c3da58641e052f53d694a80657258df33.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} 2\\left(\\cos\\frac{2\\pi}{7}+\\cos\\frac{4\\pi}{7}+\\cos\\frac{6\\pi}{7}\\right)&amp;=-1\\\\ \\cos\\frac{2\\pi}{7}+\\cos\\frac{4\\pi}{7}+\\cos\\frac{6\\pi}{7}&amp;=-\\frac12. \\end{align*}\" width=\"291\" height=\"86\" />\nNote that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/d/cfdfba2c5258e27f053f5a3a495e66efba6870a1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\theta=\\frac{2\\pi}{7},\\frac{4\\pi}{7},\\frac{6\\pi}{7}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"120\" height=\"37\" /> are roots of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9e9f02c782674692e8e67212d21939845ab480b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\cos\\theta+\\cos(2\\theta)+\\cos(3\\theta)=-\\frac12, \\hspace{15mm} (\\bigstar)\\]\" width=\"353\" height=\"37\" /> as they can be verified either algebraically (by the identity <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/e/0ce27b62fbc06d194f8ad989637d9d3865263666.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos\\theta=\\cos(-\\theta)=\\cos(2\\pi-\\theta)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"235\" height=\"18\" />) or geometrically (by the graph below).\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/0/0c0b46ea12dd65cdf8d2ccd13731e8677480a5d1.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] /* Made by MRENTHUSIASM */ size(200);   int xMin = -2; int xMax = 2; int yMin = -2; int yMax = 2; int numRays = 24;  //Draws a polar grid that goes out to a number of circles  //equal to big, with numRays specifying the number of rays:  void polarGrid(int big, int numRays)  {   for (int i = 1; i &lt; big+1; ++i)   {     draw(Circle((0,0),i), gray+linewidth(0.4));   }   for(int i=0;i&lt;numRays;++i)    draw(rotate(i*360/numRays)*((-big,0)--(big,0)), gray+linewidth(0.4)); }  //Draws the horizontal gridlines void horizontalLines() {   for (int i = yMin+1; i &lt; yMax; ++i)   {     draw((xMin,i)--(xMax,i), mediumgray+linewidth(0.4));   } }  //Draws the vertical gridlines void verticalLines() {   for (int i = xMin+1; i &lt; xMax; ++i)   {     draw((i,yMin)--(i,yMax), mediumgray+linewidth(0.4));   } }  horizontalLines(); verticalLines(); polarGrid(xMax,numRays); draw((xMin,0)--(xMax,0),black+linewidth(1.5),EndArrow(5)); draw((0,yMin)--(0,yMax),black+linewidth(1.5),EndArrow(5)); label(&quot;Re&quot;,(xMax,0),(2,0)); label(&quot;Im&quot;,(0,yMax),(0,2));  //The n such that we&#39;re taking the nth roots of unity int n = 7;  pair A[]; for(int i = 0; i &lt;= n-1; i+=1) {   A[i] = rotate(360*i/n)*(1,0); }  label(&quot;$1$&quot;,A[0],NE, UnFill); for(int i =1; i &lt; n; ++i) {    label(&quot;$e^{\\frac{&quot; +string(2i)+&quot;\\pi i}{&quot; + string(n) + &quot;}}$&quot;,A[i],dir(A[i]), UnFill); }  draw(Circle((0,0),1),red);  for(int i = 0; i&lt; n; ++i) dot(A[i],linewidth(3.5));  [/asy]\" width=\"335\" height=\"325\" />\nLet <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/1/011cadec5d2631777d196a379d45848099cbb62d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=\\cos\\theta.$\" width=\"74\" height=\"13\" /> We apply the Double-Angle and Triple-Angle Identities to rewrite <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/5/875816dba06e32edf79fcfbb793af13f73bdca9c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(\\bigstar)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"29\" height=\"18\" /> in terms of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/0/6d0382f3585219947b495ac2262a81b7b0c40db2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"17\" height=\"13\" /> and then rearrange:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/2/7/d270f215641c9593948c96c03ba4f4968e44c8ec.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} x+\\left(2x^2-1\\right)+\\left(4x^3-3x\\right)&amp;=-\\frac12 \\\\ 4x^3+2x^2-2x-\\frac12&amp;=0 \\\\ x^3+\\frac12 x^2 - \\frac12 x - \\frac18 &amp;= 0. \\end{align*}\" width=\"263\" height=\"123\" />\nRecall that the roots are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/8/5/285c8ad94c56deb9afd54a422ae0fc9fb90a7caf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=\\cos\\frac{2\\pi}{7},\\cos\\frac{4\\pi}{7},\\cos\\frac{6\\pi}{7}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"208\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p>Therefore, we obtain <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/1/a/11a9ebb6abaa110105596c25227a3fbfdb353255.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a,b,c)=\\left(\\frac12,-\\frac12,-\\frac18\\right),$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"196\" height=\"43\" /> from which <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/c/bacbec39215e5064ddb7180a2be73ae73749671e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$abc=\\boxed{\\textbf{(D) }\\frac{1}{32}}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"122\" height=\"48\" />\n</p><p>~MRENTHUSIASM (inspired by Peeyush Pandaya et al)\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.28Trigonometric_Identities.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(Trigonometric_Identities)\">Solution 3 (Trigonometric Identities)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (Trigonometric Identities)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We solve for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/b/f3b28547efd22be1c4a05fa193cd7038fc65d71b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a,b,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"29\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> separately:\n</p>\n<ol style=\"margin-left: 1.5em;\">\n  <li>Solve for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/0/7b0ab92f0755c7535c29925847f9d2b2a2330d2b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a:$\" width=\"18\" height=\"8\" /> By Vieta's Formulas, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/e/5/7e50f3b75f3e57fca68a7ccb9e70bfcd3e6aa572.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = - \\left( \\cos \\frac{2\\pi}7 + \\cos \\frac{4\\pi}7 + \\cos \\frac{6\\pi}7 \\right).$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"286\" height=\"45\" /><p>\nThe real parts of the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />th roots of unity are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/2/1d244e8b34090f9f1aa746255e3e97adda2d1652.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1, \\cos \\frac{2\\pi}7, \\cos \\frac{4\\pi}7, \\cos \\frac{6\\pi}7, \\cos \\frac{8\\pi}7, \\cos \\frac{10\\pi}7, \\cos \\frac{12\\pi}7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"383\" height=\"37\" /> and they sum to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/4/604c735470dd0152ca1cff75fe26eadf5cef7f49.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> </p><p>\nNote that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/9/369107ca6ccdee14ca8f312e7fbeb36795cbb2f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos\\theta=\\cos(2\\pi-\\theta)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"149\" height=\"18\" /> for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/6/79607326260cf94d825a16e94c1c1b1a8af24db6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\theta.$\" width=\"12\" height=\"13\" /> Excluding <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/f/5bf27edd6ee0c25241392922eca9b9c9144f4d73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"16\" height=\"17\" /> the other six roots add to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/c/fccce4342acebef56eb25564e67d4dfa91828ddf.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2\\left(\\cos \\frac{2\\pi}7 + \\cos \\frac{4\\pi}7 + \\cos \\frac{6\\pi}7\\right) = -1,\\]\" width=\"288\" height=\"43\" /> from which <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/e/1de5065c775773dbd9c46521749826170f9f7776.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\cos \\frac{2\\pi}7 + \\cos \\frac{4\\pi}7 + \\cos \\frac{6\\pi}7 = -\\frac12.\\]\" width=\"253\" height=\"37\" />\nTherefore, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/2/e423b67f29758f723241f19d8dfc49feda138d6c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = -\\left(-\\frac12\\right) = \\frac12.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"149\" height=\"45\" /></p></li><p class=\"mw-empty-elt\">\n  </p><li>Solve for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/9/339571d86cf6ba1241aa502a0ce825fbecd14630.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b:$\" width=\"16\" height=\"12\" /> By Vieta's Formulas, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/1/821802b5149d643d63f9766850cff8f55ceeffea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b = \\cos \\frac{2\\pi}7 \\cos \\frac{4\\pi}7 + \\cos \\frac{2\\pi}7 \\cos \\frac{6\\pi}7 + \\cos \\frac{4\\pi}7 \\cos \\frac{6\\pi}7.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"401\" height=\"38\" /><p>\nNote that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/7/107b06e842492ef4f42b0c3028c42207c9fa6989.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos \\alpha \\cos \\beta = \\frac{ \\cos \\left(\\alpha + \\beta\\right) + \\cos \\left(\\alpha - \\beta\\right) }{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"306\" height=\"40\" /> for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/f/10f32377ac67d94f764f12a15ea987e88c85d3e1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\alpha$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/7/6/d768e6d509507653c997a03c8573788b8740ef7d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\beta.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"14\" height=\"16\" /> Therefore, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/1/ba1cadf31da59872fa6f3f3a9f59da44759c6d54.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[b=\\frac{\\cos \\frac{6\\pi}7 + \\cos \\frac{2\\pi}7}2 + \\frac{\\cos \\frac{6\\pi}7 + \\cos \\frac{4\\pi}7}2 + \\frac{\\cos \\frac{4\\pi}7 + \\cos \\frac{2\\pi}7}2=\\cos \\frac{2\\pi}7 + \\cos \\frac{4\\pi}7 + \\cos \\frac{6\\pi}7=-\\frac12.\\]\" width=\"677\" height=\"41\" /></p></li>\n  <li>Solve for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/8/5d81ffe14dc65d342d075662e3f3bd00898dbd2e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c:$\" width=\"16\" height=\"8\" /> By Vieta's Formulas, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/c/0ecb7418a0cbdb2009311c9fb577d2bea9c15561.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c = -\\cos \\frac{2\\pi}7 \\cos \\frac{4\\pi}7 \\cos \\frac{6\\pi}7=-\\cos \\frac{2\\pi}7 \\cos \\frac{4\\pi}7 \\cos \\frac{8\\pi}7.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"418\" height=\"38\" /> <p>\nWe multiply both sides by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/c/0ecae4a72d0121d7fac4a7dd34b4497b450b685a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8 \\sin{\\frac{2\\pi}{7}},$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"68\" height=\"38\" /> then repeatedly apply the angle addition formula for sine:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/b/e/dbe0d56199cc104a248552e6984ab94825f88f82.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} c \\cdot 8 \\sin{\\frac{2\\pi}{7}} &amp;= -8 \\sin{\\frac{2\\pi}{7}} \\cos \\frac{2\\pi}7 \\cos \\frac{4\\pi}7 \\cos \\frac{8\\pi}7 \\\\ &amp;= -4 \\sin \\frac{4\\pi}7 \\cos \\frac{4\\pi}7 \\cos \\frac{8\\pi}7 \\\\ &amp;= -2 \\sin \\frac{8\\pi}7 \\cos \\frac{8\\pi}7 \\\\ &amp;= -\\sin \\frac{16\\pi}7 \\\\ &amp;= -\\sin \\frac{2\\pi}7. \\end{align*}\" width=\"344\" height=\"209\" />\nTherefore, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/a/f3a7ba88abdb29020134c4c349f6f2de90c17368.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c = -\\frac18.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"66\" height=\"38\" /></p><p class=\"mw-empty-elt\">\n</p></li>\n</ol>\n<p>Finally, the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/7/2a77f57d8b45fe1603792f6f63fd4d0b94148a62.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$abc=\\frac12\\cdot\\left(-\\frac12\\right)\\cdot\\left(-\\frac18\\right)=\\boxed{\\textbf{(D) }\\frac{1}{32}}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"296\" height=\"49\" />\n</p><p>~Tucker\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_4_.28Product-to-Sum_Identity.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4_(Product-to-Sum_Identity)\">Solution 4 (Product-to-Sum Identity)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4 (Product-to-Sum Identity)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Note that the sum of the roots of unity equal zero, so the sum of their real parts equal zero, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/9/e19a1966ab785e43ffd376a89238eb6372b9cc21.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\operatorname{Re}\\left(\\omega^{m}\\right) = \\operatorname{Re}\\left(\\omega^{-m}\\right).$\" style=\"vertical-align: -7px\" width=\"173\" height=\"23\" /> We have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/b/1ababe2f31cd00300aae315fa8de290690bbb107.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\cos \\frac{2 \\pi}{7} + \\cos \\frac{4 \\pi}{7} + \\cos \\frac{6 \\pi}{7} = \\frac12(0 - \\cos 0) = -\\frac12,\\]\" width=\"373\" height=\"37\" /> so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/5/415568c13a3e40a5c11180a1394fa0d51b8092cd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = \\frac{1}{2}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"50\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p>By the Product-to-Sum Identity, we have \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/a/5aa9c6ef16edd86f1f0fd2f11be476711b651767.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} \\cos \\frac{2 \\pi}{7} \\cos \\frac{4 \\pi}{7} + \\cos \\frac{2 \\pi}{7} \\cos \\frac{6 \\pi}{7} + \\cos \\frac{4 \\pi}{7} \\cos \\frac{6 \\pi}{7} &amp;= \\frac{1}{2} \\left(2 \\cos \\frac{2 \\pi}{7} + \\cos \\frac{4 \\pi}{7} + \\cos \\frac{6 \\pi}{7} + \\cos \\frac{8 \\pi}{7} + \\cos \\frac{10 \\pi}{7}\\right) \\\\ &amp;= \\frac{1}{2}\\left(2 \\cos \\frac{2 \\pi}{7} + 2 \\cos \\frac{4 \\pi}{7} + 2 \\cos \\frac{6 \\pi}{7}\\right) \\\\ &amp;= \\cos \\frac{2 \\pi}{7} + \\cos \\frac{4 \\pi}{7} + \\cos \\frac{6 \\pi}{7} \\\\ &amp;= -\\frac{1}{2}, \\end{align*}\" width=\"792\" height=\"178\" />\nso <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/8/7284ab3358783b127d40908b320edee13d6db341.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b = -\\frac{1}{2}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"63\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p>By the Product-to-Sum Identity, we have \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/c/3ac6f0fa9d156bc7457d13e831d322a733938a4c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} \\cos \\frac{2 \\pi}{7} \\cos \\frac{4 \\pi}{7} \\cos \\frac{6 \\pi}{7} &amp;= \\frac{1}{2}\\cos \\frac{6 \\pi}{7}\\left(\\cos \\frac{2 \\pi}{7} + \\cos \\frac{6 \\pi}{7}\\right) \\\\ &amp;= \\frac{1}{4}\\left(\\cos \\frac{4 \\pi}{7} +  \\cos \\frac{8 \\pi}{7}\\right) + \\frac{1}{4}\\left(1 + \\cos \\frac{12 \\pi}{7}\\right) \\\\ &amp;= \\frac{1}{4}\\left(1 + \\cos\\frac{2\\pi}{7} + \\cos \\frac{4\\pi}{7} + \\cos \\frac{6\\pi}{7}\\right) \\\\ &amp;= \\frac{1}{8}, \\end{align*}\" width=\"504\" height=\"185\" />\nso <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/0/630e6d64cb3a307600087439053e7b2f6605ced8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c = -\\frac{1}{8}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"66\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>Finally, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/c/bacbec39215e5064ddb7180a2be73ae73749671e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$abc=\\boxed{\\textbf{(D) }\\frac{1}{32}}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"122\" height=\"48\" />\n</p><p>~ccx09\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Easy_Video_Solution_by_Scholars_Foundation_Without_Complex_Numbers_and_Euler.27s_Identity_.28Using_Trigonometry_.2B_Vieta.27s_Formula.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Easy_Video_Solution_by_Scholars_Foundation_Without_Complex_Numbers_and_Euler's_Identity_(Using_Trigonometry_+_Vieta's_Formula)\">Easy Video Solution by Scholars Foundation Without Complex Numbers and Euler's Identity (Using Trigonometry + Vieta's Formula)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Easy Video Solution by Scholars Foundation Without Complex Numbers and Euler&#39;s Identity (Using Trigonometry + Vieta&#39;s Formula)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/m4N4KN6_tA0\">https://youtu.be/m4N4KN6_tA0</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_by_OmegaLearn_.28Euler.27s_Identity_.2B_Vieta.27s_Formula.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_OmegaLearn_(Euler's_Identity_+_Vieta's_Formula)\">Video Solution by OmegaLearn (Euler's Identity + Vieta's Formula)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by OmegaLearn (Euler&#39;s Identity + Vieta&#39;s Formula)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/Im_WTIK0tss\">https://youtu.be/Im_WTIK0tss</a>\n</p><p>~ pi_is_3.14\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_grogg007\">Video Solution by <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=User:Grogg007\" title=\"User:Grogg007\">grogg007</a></span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by grogg007\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=hP4cpuAszLo\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=hP4cpuAszLo</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"2\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12A\" title=\"2021 AMC 12A\">2021 AMC 12A</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12A_Problems\" title=\"2021 AMC 12A Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12A_Answer_Key\" title=\"2021 AMC 12A Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_21\" title=\"2021 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 21\">Problem 21</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_23\" title=\"2021 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 23\">Problem 23</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2021 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2021 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2021 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2021 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2021 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2021 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2021 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2021 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2021 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2021 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2021 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2021 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2021 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2021 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2021 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 15\">15</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_16\" title=\"2021 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 16\">16</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_17\" title=\"2021 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 17\">17</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_18\" title=\"2021 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 18\">18</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_19\" title=\"2021 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 19\">19</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_20\" title=\"2021 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 20\">20</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_21\" title=\"2021 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 21\">21</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">22</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_23\" title=\"2021 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 23\">23</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_24\" title=\"2021 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 24\">24</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_25\" title=\"2021 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 25\">25</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AMC_12_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AMC 12 Problems and Solutions\"> All AMC 12 Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017141156\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.051 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.069 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 458/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 2298/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 158/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 17448/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   13.292      1 -total\n 56.33%    7.488      1 Template:AMC12_box\n 42.10%    5.596      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:19797:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017141156 and revision id 289562. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}